To write Burst-compatible code for parallel processing, you need to use Unity's Job System and Burst Compiler together. Here's an example of a simple parallel job that calculates the sum of an array of integers:

```csharp
[BurstCompile]
public struct SumJob : IJob
{
    [ReadOnly]
    public NativeArray<int> data;
    public NativeArray<int> result;

    public void Execute()
    {
        int sum = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < data.Length; i++)
        {
            sum += data[i];
        }
        result[0] = sum;
    }
}

// Usage
NativeArray<int> data = new NativeArray<int>(1000, Allocator.TempJob);
NativeArray<int> result = new NativeArray<int>(1, Allocator.TempJob);
SumJob sumJob = new SumJob { data = data, result = result };
JobHandle handle = sumJob.Schedule();
handle.Complete();
Console.WriteLine(result[0]);
```
